--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/skills/spec-report/report.org
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+#+TITLE: /spec-report report
+
+* status
+Implemented. SKILL.md covers every requirement in the spec, and
+nothing in the repo contradicts it. Two details for markdown specs
+rest on assumptions SKILL.md makes, which the spec could confirm.
+
+* conflicts
+None. The spec has no =:conflict-plan:= headings.
+
+Evidence:
+- Each requirement below maps to a section of SKILL.md that does what
+  it says, and none of them does anything the spec rules out.
+- =grep -rln conflict-plan= over the repo's org and md files finds
+  only spec.org, at spec.org:25, where the tag is defined.
+
+* conflict plans that can be removed
+None. The spec contains no =:conflict-plan:= headings to remove.
+
+Evidence: spec.org has no headings at all; its only org markup above
+the list is =#+TITLE= (spec.org:1).
+
+* not implemented
+Nothing the spec requires is missing. Two details are implemented on
+assumptions, since the spec does not settle them.
+
+** conflict plans in markdown specs
+Implemented on an assumption; ready to implement once confirmed.
+
+spec.org:24-25 defines a conflict resolution plan as a heading
+"tagged with =:conflict-plan:=". Heading tags are an org feature, but
+spec.org:7-8 also accepts =SPEC.md= and =SPEC--*.md=. SKILL.md:61-64
+assumes a markdown plan is a heading whose text ends with
+=:conflict-plan:=.
+
+Question for the spec:
+1. How does a markdown spec mark a conflict resolution plan? Is a
+   heading ending in =:conflict-plan:= right?
+
+** report name for =SPEC--*.md=
+Implemented by the rule; the example disagrees.
+
+spec.org:20 gives the rule =s/^spec/report/=, which SKILL.md:31-36
+applies with case kept, so =SPEC--NAME.md= gives =REPORT--NAME.md=.
+The examples at spec.org:18-19 list =REPORT--*.org= instead, and
+=report--**.org= with a doubled star. Running the naming command from
+SKILL.md:33-36 on each spec form gives:
+
+#+begin_example
+spec.org -> report.org
+SPEC.md -> REPORT.md
+spec--cli.org -> report--cli.org
+SPEC--cli.md -> REPORT--cli.md
+#+end_example
+
+Question for the spec:
+2. Should spec.org:19 read =report--*.org= and =REPORT--*.md=, to
+   match the rule at spec.org:20?
+
+* implemented
+** the skill (spec.org:3-4)
+=.claude/skills/spec-report/SKILL.md= exists, added in b3c3d63d
+"claude/skills/spec-report: Add the spec-report skill". It sets
+=disable-model-invocation: true= (SKILL.md:8).
+
+** the report (spec.org:3)
+This file, written by following SKILL.md against spec.org and
+committed as SKILL.md:140-157 describes.
+
+** reading the spec from args (spec.org:7-8)
+SKILL.md:14-16 takes the spec path from =$ARGUMENTS=. SKILL.md:26-28
+accepts the four basename forms from spec.org:7-8 and stops on any
+other.
+
+** analysis of the working copy (spec.org:9-11)
+SKILL.md:77-83 judges the working copy as checked out, not trunk, and
+bases findings on implementation and documentation. SKILL.md:90-95
+asks for each requirement to be followed to the code that carries it
+out, with read-only subagents for a large spec.
+
+** notes as context only (spec.org:12-15)
+SKILL.md:85-88 treats notes as context and never as evidence, naming
+=zib/= and text-only files that neither implement nor document the
+behavior.
+
+** commit history (spec.org:16-17)
+SKILL.md:66-73 reads the history of the spec and its directory with
+=jj log=, for context, direction, and decisions.
+
+** sibling report and its name (spec.org:18-20)
+SKILL.md:30-40 names the report by =s/^spec/report/=, keeping case,
+in the spec's directory and format. See the naming output above.
+
+** report sections (spec.org:21-38)
+SKILL.md:117-130 lists the five sections in the order the spec gives
+them: status, conflicts with whether a plan covers each, removable
+plans, what is not implemented, and what is implemented.
+SKILL.md:97-113 defines the classification, the check of each
+=:conflict-plan:= against the conflicts found, and the "ready to
+implement" and "not ready to implement" verdicts with questions.
+
+** no plan in the report (spec.org:36-37)
+SKILL.md:21 and SKILL.md:137-138 forbid an implementation plan in the
+report.
+
+** evidence (spec.org:39-40)
+SKILL.md:132-135 requires evidence for every claim outside the status
+section: spec lines, =path:line= references, commits, and command
+output. SKILL.md:120-121 exempts the status.
+
+** commit, overwriting the report (spec.org:41-44)
+SKILL.md:117 overwrites the report in full, and SKILL.md:142-150
+commits it alone, then checks the commit from outside
+(SKILL.md:152-157).
+
+** sclr reports (spec.org:45-47)
+SKILL.md:42-54 moves an existing =report.org= to =sclr-report.org=
+in its own commit when a sibling =lore.org= exists. =src/portia= and
+=src/cell= both have a =lore.org= beside their =spec.org=, so this
+applies to them.
